From 1be55375f3a1887217db6a457f63103131346e40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GB-build k14 <k14@builder.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 101/103] drm/nouveau: don't set ignore_hotplug when the bridge
 has _PR3

nouveau_pmops_runtime_suspend() calls pci_ignore_hotplug() on every
runtime suspend.  The flag is never cleared again and is propagated to
the upstream port: pciehp then ignores every later slot event of that
port, and acpiphp's trim_stale_devices() treats the GPU as alive.  It is
only needed when the GPU's power is cut behind the PCI core's back, i.e.
the Optimus/_DSM path.

When the upstream bridge may enter D3 and has ACPI power resources
(_PR3), nouveau already skips the Optimus _DSM (nouveau_dsm_pci_probe())
and the PCI core powers the slot down itself through the port's runtime
PM, around which pciehp disables and re-checks its events.  On such
platforms a genuine removal must still be seen; on the Surface Book 3
the GPU sits in the detachable base and after one nouveau runtime
suspend a later base removal is never handled.

Skip pci_ignore_hotplug() in that case, as amdgpu did in commit
ceb4de67c960 ("drm/amdgpu: no need to call pci_ignore_hotplug for
_PR3"), and say once in the log which path is in use.  Only do so when
pciehp really quiesces: it masks the slot interrupt across the port's
D3cold only if the OS owns PME (pciehp_disable_interrupt()), otherwise
the link-down would be handled as a removal.  Without native PCIe
hotplug, pciehp is not involved and acpiphp only acts on ACPI
notifications.  pci_find_host_bridge() is open-coded because it is not
exported by this GKI kernel.

Local patch N1 for the Googlebook SB3 k14 kernel (not upstream).
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c
index d05da2d..65ae3b8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c
@@ -1112,6 +1112,31 @@ nouveau_pmops_runtime(void)
 	return nouveau_runtime_pm == 1;
 }
 
+/*
+ * True when the PCI core, not nouveau's _DSM path, cuts power to the GPU and the
+ * upstream port's hotplug driver copes with that:
+ *  - the bridge may enter D3 and has ACPI power resources (_PR3), the test
+ *    nouveau_dsm_pci_probe() uses to skip the Optimus _DSM, and
+ *  - the OS owns PME, so pciehp masks its slot interrupt while the port is
+ *    powered down (pciehp_disable_interrupt()), or PCIe native hotplug is not
+ *    in use at all (acpiphp only acts on ACPI notifications).
+ */
+static bool
+nouveau_pr3_power_managed(struct pci_dev *pdev)
+{
+	struct pci_dev *bridge = pci_upstream_bridge(pdev);
+	struct pci_bus *bus = pdev->bus;
+	struct pci_host_bridge *host;
+
+	if (!bridge || !bridge->bridge_d3 || !pci_pr3_present(bridge))
+		return false;
+
+	while (bus->parent)	/* pci_find_host_bridge(), which is not exported */
+		bus = bus->parent;
+	host = to_pci_host_bridge(bus->bridge);
+	return host->native_pme || !host->native_pcie_hotplug;
+}
+
 static int
 nouveau_pmops_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
@@ -1128,7 +1153,20 @@ nouveau_pmops_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	ret = nouveau_do_suspend(drm, true);
 	pci_save_state(pdev);
 	pci_disable_device(pdev);
-	pci_ignore_hotplug(pdev);
+	/*
+	 * pci_ignore_hotplug() is sticky: nothing clears it again, pciehp then
+	 * ignores every later event of the upstream port and acpiphp treats the
+	 * device as alive.  It is meant for GPUs whose power is cut behind the
+	 * PCI core's back (_DSM/Optimus).  With _PR3 on the upstream bridge the
+	 * PCI core powers the slot down itself and the hotplug drivers quiesce
+	 * around that, so keep hotplug enabled: a real removal (e.g. a detached
+	 * Surface Book base) must still be handled.  Same as amdgpu commit
+	 * ceb4de67c960 ("drm/amdgpu: no need to call pci_ignore_hotplug for _PR3").
+	 */
+	if (nouveau_pr3_power_managed(pdev))
+		dev_info_once(dev, "runtime PM through ACPI _PR3, hotplug left enabled\n");
+	else
+		pci_ignore_hotplug(pdev);
 	pci_set_power_state(pdev, PCI_D3cold);
 	drm->dev->switch_power_state = DRM_SWITCH_POWER_DYNAMIC_OFF;
 	return ret;
